B.a6E=new A.fo("The production problem","AI systems fail in ways that normal software dashboards do not catch quickly enough. A response can be fluent, confident, and still wrong. In customer support, that means a policy mistake. In social media, it means inflated claims. In finance, it means unsupported analysis. A self-healing agent treats these failures as operational incidents instead of isolated bad outputs.")
B.a6K=new A.fo("The healing loop","The core loop is intentionally simple: capture the answer, evaluate it, diagnose the failure mode, rewrite the prompt, verify the new behavior, and publish evidence. This turns a subjective quality complaint into a traceable workflow.")
B.a6I=new A.fo("Why the architecture matters","The agent does not only generate answers. It observes its own behavior through Phoenix traces, retrieves those traces through MCP, uses Gemini to judge and repair failures, and then pushes updated prompts back into the live agents.")
B.QS=s([B.a6E,B.a6K,B.a6I],t.yq)
B.a8f=new A.qT("Self-Healing Agent Architecture","Architecture","7 min","A visual explanation of how the dashboard, FastAPI backend, Phoenix MCP, Gemini, and the healing loop work together.",B.QS,!0)
B.a6G=new A.fo("Trace first, diagnose second","A healing system needs more than logs. It needs input, output, span name, timestamp, use case, scores, and run metadata. Phoenix traces provide the evidence trail for the agent.")
B.a6M=new A.fo("What judges should see","A judge should be able to open Phoenix Traces and immediately see the project, MCP retrieval status, trace IDs, span names, scores, and before or after status.")
B.a6N=new A.fo("Why MCP matters","Phoenix MCP turns observability into an agent-readable interface. Instead of only showing traces to humans, the system can retrieve trace evidence during the repair loop.")
B.Pl=s([B.a6G,B.a6M,B.a6N],t.yq)
B.a8c=new A.qT("Phoenix Traces as the Agent Memory for Repair","Observability","5 min","How trace evidence connects one AI output to the healing action that follows.",B.Pl,!1)
B.a6L=new A.fo("The risk","Support agents are high-risk because users treat their answers as policy. A weak prompt can invent refund terms, shipping guarantees, or escalation paths.")
B.a6D=new A.fo("The repair","The support workflow evaluates the answer against FAQ-grounded expectations. When hallucination is high or relevance is weak, the system diagnoses the pattern and rewrites the prompt toward grounded behavior.")
B.a6C=new A.fo("Product value","The judge can ask a policy question, see the initial response, trigger healing, and inspect the before and after report.")
B.PR=s([B.a6L,B.a6D,B.a6C],t.yq)
B.a8d=new A.qT("Use Case: Customer Support That Stops Guessing","Customer Support","6 min","How the support agent moves from confident guessing to FAQ-grounded answers.",B.PR,!1)
B.a6B=new A.fo("The risk","Social media generation often rewards punchy language. That is exactly where hallucination becomes expensive.")
B.a6J=new A.fo("The repair","The social media healer compares the brief to the generated post, scores hallucination and relevance, and patches the prompt with stricter grounding rules.")
B.a6H=new A.fo("Product value","The post workflow shows a clean business story for hackathon judging: the agent catches exaggerated language, rewrites its own instructions, and produces a safer post.")
B.Q2=s([B.a6B,B.a6J,B.a6H],t.yq)
B.a8e=new A.qT("Use Case: Social Media Posts Without Inflated Claims","Social Media","5 min","Why post generation needs claim discipline, not just creativity.",B.Q2,!1)
B.a6A=new A.fo("The risk","Investment answers are high-stakes because confident language can be mistaken for advice.")
B.a6O=new A.fo("The repair","The investment workflow combines SEC context with evaluation of grounding, risk flags, and answer quality.")
B.a6F=new A.fo("Product value","This use case shows why self-healing is not only for chatbots. The same trace, score, diagnose, patch, and verify loop can protect factual workflows.")
B.Pu=s([B.a6A,B.a6O,B.a6F],t.yq)
B.a8b=new A.qT("Use Case: Investment Analysis Grounded in SEC Evidence","Investment","7 min","How SEC-grounded analysis reduces unsupported financial conclusions.",B.Pu,!1)
